cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mcpmap: an empirical risk study of the public MCP server ecosystem"
message: >-
  If you use this instrument or its figures, please cite it, and state the
  taxonomy version alongside any capability figure you quote.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The mcpmap contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mt211211/alpha"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - agent security
  - supply chain
  - measurement study
abstract: >-
  mcpmap measures the risk distribution of publicly published Model Context
  Protocol servers and how that distribution drifts over time, from published
  metadata only. Capabilities are inferred from tool names, descriptions and
  schema keys; the inference is scored against a hand-labelled set that ships
  with the instrument, so capability figures can be published as measured lower
  bounds rather than assertions. The instrument never installs, launches,
  connects to or invokes an MCP server.
